    "title": "News of God's Grace: A Mountain Prayer Experience",
    "date": "24 March 2024",
    "category": "testimonies",
    "author": "Evangelist Allan Mukwasi",
    "excerpt": "On the 8th of December 2019, I was diagnosed with influenza...",
    "content": "On December 10 at 5:47 PM, eight of us – Preacher Nobhula, Secretaries Mutonhore, Matienga, Madongorere, Jerera, Somerai, Dreamer Manyengavana, and myself – set out for Yanas Mountain in Ras Al Khaimah. Our journey was quiet, filled only with hymns. In spirit, we were already climbing, each note drawing us nearer to God's presence.\n\nWe arrived around 7:00 PM and, since we had no women or children with us, we climbed straight to the top. It took about 45 minutes. When we reached the summit, we began with humble confession. The Holy Spirit was present, and our Dreamers received visions and prophecy, each message guiding those present. As we worshipped, it felt as if heaven joined our chorus.\n\nWhile we were still praying, the sound of cars approached the mountain base. Soon, over 30 vehicles had surrounded our parked car. I encouraged the brethren, \"Let's sing louder so that those below know we are worshipping.\" The vehicles began circling the mountain, honking loudly. I decided to go down and meet them.\n\nHalfway down, I met two Arab men in white garments. I called out \"Mafi Mushkila\" (No problem), but they kept their distance. When I reached the base, more than 25 men surrounded me. They spoke rapidly in Arabic, but I simply replied, \"No Arabic, Mafi Mushkila. Only praying up there.\"\n\nI told them, \"My name is Allan Mukwasi. I am here with seven brethren in Christ. We are members of the African Apostolic Church under the divine leadership of Paul Mwazha of Africa. We came for special prayers, and these garments are our consecrated prayer attire.\"\n\nThe atmosphere changed to joy and laughter. One elder, Sunil, offered us a quieter place to pray and asked if we needed food or warmth. I explained we were fasting and had all we needed. Before parting, they asked us to pray for their community. I took Sunil's contact and apologised for any distress caused, assuring them we would seek permission in the future. They received this with goodwill.\n\nI returned to the mountain top, and we continued in prayer with renewed unity and divine purpose. What began as tension ended in peace and fellowship. God turned a moment of misunderstanding into news of His grace, proving that fear yields to faith and strangers can become friends through His presence."
