    "author": "The African Apostolic Church Publicity",
    "excerpt": "After years of infertility, a dream of Mutumwa Paul Mwazha...",
    "content": "I was married in 2003 but could not conceive. I had a dream in which Mutumwa Paul Mwazha came to me, flying, and landed next to my bed. He told me to join the church and gave me directions to find it. I followed the instructions in the dream and went to the church, where I shared my dream and my problem with the elders.\n\nThey prayed for me the first time I came. On another day, I joined the queue for prayers, but the elders removed me from the line, took me aside, and prayed for me again. They told me, nokutenda uchabatsirwa (by faith you will be helped).\n\nA month later, I became pregnant, and we named the child Nokutenda. Later, in January, my husband was struck by lightning. I prayed, and when he came home, his socks were burnt, but his feet were untouched. I thank God for the help I received through His messenger, Mutumwa Mwazha."
